the topic for our discussion is faith  and globalization but what do we mean by  faith and what do we mean by  globalization how do we understand faith  in the world today well we use faith in  plural we mean multiple faiths and we  use faith in plural in order to signal  that we are not interested in some  abstraction called faith but rather in  concrete religious traditions we're  interested in how people are shaped by  these traditions how people to say it in  this way inhabit those traditions how  these traditions shaped concrete lives  of people of course we are also  interested in kind of diffuse forms of  religiosity but sometimes people  describe as smorgasbord religiosity  especially appearing in the Western  countries that too is a force that  shapes people's lives so that's how we  will treat the term faith we will also  explore what is the best way to  understand the processes of  globalization now this is a very  contested field and many theories of  globalization's are in play we will  discuss those various theories and try  to find appropriate ways and through  which to access that very complex  phenomenon and indeed because both  faiths and globalization processes are  such complex phenomena we will attend to  the interdisciplinary character of the  search to understand these phenomena  faith and also globalization this is the  place where scholars from various  disciplines and fields can come together  and look at the phenomenon that shape  the world today in a conversational way  mutually enriching each other's  perspective
 

